      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The problem is to find the mean of the set $\\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\}$ given that the median is 9.\n\n1. **Determine the median position:**\n   Since the set has an even number of elements (5 elements), the median will be the average of the 3rd and 4th elements. According to the problem, the median is 9. Therefore, the average of the 3rd and 4th elements must be 9.\n\n2. **Set up the equation for the median:**\n   The 3rd element is \\(n + 6\\) and the 4th element is \\(n + 9\\). The average of these two elements is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(n + 6) + (n + 9)}{2} = \\frac{2n + 15}{2}\n   \\]\n   Given that this average is 9, we can set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2n + 15}{2} = 9\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(n\\):**\n   Multiply both sides of the equation by 2 to clear the fraction:\n   \\[\n   2n + 15 = 18\n   \\]\n   Subtract 15 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   2n = 3\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 2:\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{3}{2}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find the elements of the set:**\n   Substitute \\(n = \\frac{3}{2}\\) into the elements of the set:\n   \\[\n   \\{n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15\\} = \\left\\{\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} + 5, \\frac{3}{2} + 6, \\frac{3}{2} + 9, \\frac{3}{2} + 15\\right\\}\n   \\]\n   Simplify each term:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\{\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{10}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{12}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{18}{2}, \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{30}{2}\\right\\} = \\left\\{\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{13}{2}, \\frac{15}{2}, \\frac{21}{2}, \\frac{33}{2}\\right\\}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the mean:**\n   The mean is the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements. First, find the sum of the elements:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{13}{2} + \\frac{15}{2} + \\frac{21}{2} + \\frac{33}{2} = \\frac{3 + 13 + 15 + 21 + 33}{2} = \\frac{85}{2}\n   \\]\n   The number of elements is 5. Therefore, the mean is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\frac{85}{2}}{5} = \\frac{85}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{85}{10} = 8.5\n   \\]\n\nThus, the mean of the set is \\(\\boxed{8.5}\\).",
