      "text": "The median is the middle value when the numbers are arranged in ascending order. Given that the set in ascending order is $\\{n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15\\}$, the median is $n+6$. According to the problem, the median is 9. We have:\n\\[ n + 6 = 9 \\]\n\nTherefore, solving for $n$:\n\\[ n = 9 - 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 3 \\]\n\nThe given set in clear terms is:\n\\[ \\{3, 3+5, 3+6, 3+9, 3+15\\} = \\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\} \\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the mean. The mean is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. So, we calculate the sum of the numbers and divide by 5:\n\\[ \\text{Sum} = 3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18 = 50 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{50}{5} = 10 \\]\n\nThus, the mean of the set is $\\boxed{10}$.",
